    "safety": "Immunosuppressive treatment can change infection risk and symptom response. Follow the specialist’s urgent plan for fever, severe breathing difficulty, chest symptoms, new neurological changes, serious rash or swelling, dehydration, pregnancy concerns, or rapidly worsening function. Do not stop steroids or other immune medicines abruptly unless the prescribing clinician directs it. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
