    "safety": "Follow the pediatric team’s condition-specific plan. Trouble breathing, blue or gray color, unresponsiveness, seizure, severe dehydration, uncontrolled bleeding, serious allergic reaction, poisoning, major injury, or a marked change in behavior or alertness may require emergency services. Never give adult medicines, change pediatric doses, or recommend fasting or supplements without pediatric review. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
