    "safety": "Every chronic condition needs a clinician-authored escalation plan. New severe symptoms should not automatically be attributed to the existing diagnosis, and sudden breathing difficulty, chest pain, one-sided weakness, major bleeding, loss of consciousness, or other emergency signs require immediate professional response. Medication changes, restrictive diets, fasting, supplements, and intense exercise should be reviewed with the treating team. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
