    "safety": "Discipline must not be secretive retaliation, reputation management, coerced confession, or a substitute for reporting crimes and safeguarding victims. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Before formal action, clarify jurisdiction, evidence, witnesses, conflicts of interest, confidentiality limits, alleged crime, victim protection, and how the accused will receive the allegation and a fair opportunity to answer. Use independent review when leaders are implicated. Record decisions and reasons, communicate only to those with a legitimate need, and define observable fruits and safeguards for any restoration.",
