    "safety": "Any suicidal thinking, inability to care for basic needs, dramatic behavioral change, or possible medical cause requires immediate, competent evaluation alongside pastoral care. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Ask directly about death wishes, suicidal thought, plan, intent, means, prior attempts, substance use, psychosis-like experiences, severe agitation, and ability to eat, sleep, work, and care for dependents. Establish who will remain present, what means will be secured, which clinician or emergency service will evaluate, and when the pastor will make the next direct contact.",
