    "safety": "Severe low or high glucose can become life-threatening. Confusion, unconsciousness, seizure, inability to swallow, serious breathing changes, persistent vomiting, or symptoms identified in the person’s emergency plan require immediate action and possibly emergency services. Follow prescribed glucagon or sick-day instructions and never give food or drink to someone who cannot swallow safely. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
