    "safety": "Treat online grooming, sexual exploitation, credible threats, stalking, sextortion, trafficking, nonconsensual intimate images, child sexual-abuse material, and imminent self-harm as safeguarding concerns rather than ordinary media-habit problems. Preserve necessary account and message information without redistributing harmful material, use official platform reporting, and contact the appropriate civil authority. If a device may be monitored by an abusive person, do not change passwords, remove tracking, or clear history until a domestic-violence advocate helps assess whether that action could increase danger. Do not abruptly remove a young person’s only safe support without building another connection. Driving, sleep deprivation, financial loss, and access to dangerous online challenges also require direct assessment and immediate practical protection.",
