    "safety": "Do not assume a new symptom is part of an existing disability or that an atypical communication style means incapacity. Emergency responders need accurate baseline information, assistive devices should remain with the person when possible, and caregivers should communicate access needs without overriding the person’s decisions. Follow individualized evacuation and medical plans. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
