    "safety": "Eating disorders can cause medical instability even when a person does not appear underweight. Fainting, chest pain, irregular heartbeat, seizure, confusion, severe weakness, uncontrolled vomiting, blood in vomit, inability to keep fluids down, acute dehydration, or suicidal intent requires emergency medical evaluation. Rapid restriction, purging, laxative misuse, severe bingeing, and compulsive exercise warrant prompt professional assessment. Do not encourage abrupt dietary changes, fasting, weigh-ins, or exercise without treatment-team direction. Protect minors and dependent adults according to law and safeguarding policy when caregivers refuse necessary care. If immediate danger is present, contact emergency services and remain with the person when safe; pastoral companionship should continue alongside medical and licensed treatment.",
    "_id": "eatingdisorders"
