    "safety": "Follow the individual seizure action plan and call emergency services when a seizure lasts longer than five minutes unless the plan specifies otherwise, repeats without recovery, occurs in water, causes injury, impairs breathing or awakening, happens during pregnancy, or is a first known seizure. Do not restrain the person or put anything in the mouth. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
