    "safety": "A caregiver who is too exhausted, ill, impaired, angry, or physically unable to provide safe care needs immediate backup rather than shame. Report suspected abuse, neglect, exploitation, medication errors, unsafe transfers, or abandonment through appropriate protective and medical channels. Call emergency services for acute danger and never leave a dependent person without a safe handoff. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
