    "safety": "Gambling crises carry elevated risk of suicide, domestic conflict, illegal borrowing, fraud, eviction, loss of food or medicine, and danger to dependents. Ask directly about thoughts of death, a suicide plan, threats, violence, child safety, stolen funds, loan sharks, and whether basic needs can be met this week. Contact emergency services for imminent danger and the National Problem Gambling Helpline for specialized support. Protect shared assets through lawful, transparent arrangements and obtain legal or financial advice before moving or concealing marital property. Do not give emergency cash without a plan that prevents it from becoming gambling funds. A spouse or family member should receive independent care and must not be made solely responsible for surveillance or recovery.",
