    "safety": "Call emergency services for possible heart-attack symptoms, collapse, severe breathing difficulty, new fainting, or symptoms the cardiology team identifies as urgent; do not drive the symptomatic person unless dispatchers direct it. Never advise stopping blood thinners, heart medicines, or implanted-device follow-up, and do not dismiss different symptoms because they do not resemble a prior event. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
