    "safety": "Hospital staff should be notified immediately of sudden breathing difficulty, new chest pain, new weakness or confusion, uncontrolled pain, bleeding, a fall, a severe medication reaction, or any abrupt change. Visitors must not alter oxygen, pumps, lines, food, fluid, positioning, restraints, or medication, and should use the call system rather than improvising care. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
