    "safety": "Seek urgent assessment for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, confusion, collapse, dehydration, blue or gray color, rapidly worsening symptoms, or condition-specific warning signs. High-risk people may need time-sensitive antiviral or other treatment, so help them contact qualified care promptly rather than recommending unproven remedies or waiting for a prayer meeting. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
