    "safety": "Heavy bleeding, severe pain, fainting, fever, signs of infection, breathing difficulty, or other acute symptoms during or after pregnancy require urgent medical assessment. Follow the obstetric clinician’s instructions and contact emergency services when danger may be immediate. Ask directly about hopelessness, thoughts of self-harm, inability to care for basic needs, traumatic flashbacks, and severe sleep disruption; connect licensed mental-health care promptly when these are present. Respect the family’s privacy and never publicly announce a pregnancy, diagnosis, loss, child’s name, or treatment without explicit permission. Do not pressure a grieving person into a memorial, testimony, baby-related setting, new pregnancy, fertility treatment, adoption, or rapid return to ministry responsibilities.",
