    "safety": "Before joint counseling or disclosure, screen each spouse privately for violence, coercive control, forced sex, threats, stalking, weapon access, retaliation, self-harm, and fear of speaking freely. An affair can be disclosed in a context where confrontation increases danger; use a qualified domestic-violence advocate and individualized safety plan when abuse is present or suspected. Medical testing may be needed for sexually transmitted infections, and pregnancy or reproductive coercion requires competent medical care. Preserve relevant financial and communication records lawfully, but do not encourage illegal surveillance or retaliation. Children should not be used as confidants, messengers, investigators, or leverage. A betrayed spouse is not required to resume cohabitation, sexual contact, financial access, or conjoint sessions before safety and truthful consent exist.",
