    "safety": "Where stalking, surveillance, threats, coercive control, or violence appear, prioritize safety and qualified intervention rather than joint communication exercises. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections.",
