    "safety": "Follow the kidney team’s urgent instructions for access bleeding or infection, severe weakness, breathing difficulty, chest symptoms, confusion, fainting, rapidly increasing swelling, or missed dialysis with concerning symptoms. Never advise skipping treatment, changing fluid limits, or using over-the-counter medicines or supplements without renal-team review. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
