    "safety": "Joint counseling is inappropriate when abuse, coercion, credible fear, serious deception, or violence prevents free speech; safety and individual accountability come first. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Screen privately for fear, coercive control, physical or sexual violence, stalking, financial restriction, threats, child danger, affairs, addiction, and retaliation before placing spouses in a joint session. Do not assign symmetrical blame where power and conduct are not symmetrical. Restoration requires freely given speech, established safety, specific repentance, consequences, and sustained fruit.",
