    "definition": "Medical trauma can follow frightening symptoms, emergency transport, invasive treatment, pain, restraint, loss of control, pregnancy complications, intensive care, or prior mistreatment. Reminders may trigger panic, avoidance, nightmares, numbness, anger, or distrust even when new care is necessary. Scripture offers compassionate presence and truthful lament; it should not be used to demand instant calm, unquestioning compliance, or silence about harmful care. Medical facts must come from the treating team and reliable health authorities, while pastoral care attends to fear, grief, worship, relationships, conscience, practical burdens, and hope. The guide therefore distinguishes suffering received from sinful responses that may arise within suffering without searching for a hidden offense to explain disease.",
