    "safety": "Fever, breathing trouble, severe pain, reduced organ function signs, wound changes, vomiting that prevents medicine, or other transplant-team warning signs need immediate contact because rejection and infection can progress quickly. Never skip or alter anti-rejection medicine, use supplements, receive live vaccines, or relax food and infection precautions without transplant-team approval. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
