    "color": "amber",
    "steps": "Begin by naming the full pornography pattern before God and a mature, same-sex helper: what is viewed or read, how often, on which devices, at what times, how it is obtained or hidden, what money is spent, and whether the material or behavior has escalated. Read 1 Corinthians 6:12-20 and Ephesians 5:3-14 in context, receiving both Christ’s cleansing and His call to walk in the light. Remove ordinary provision today: surrender hidden accounts and devices, cancel paid access, place screens in shared spaces, establish filtered and reported internet access, and plan for predictable times of fatigue, loneliness, anger, boredom, rejection, or travel. Tell every necessary truth without minimizing, blaming a spouse, or demanding immediate reassurance. Build a written response for temptation that includes leaving the setting, contacting a named person, praying specific truth, and moving into an embodied act of service or fellowship. Before the next conversation, record each temptation and response without graphic detail, identify one lie pornography promised and one cost it concealed, and schedule the next accountable review. If married, pursue guided disclosure and separate care for the betrayed spouse; do not use confession to transfer the burden of managing your recovery. If a lapse occurs, report it promptly, restore safeguards, learn from the path into it, and continue repentance rather than converting shame into another excuse to hide.",
