    "safety": "Use the obstetric team’s urgent instructions and seek immediate assessment for heavy bleeding, severe pain, seizure, fainting, trouble breathing, chest pain, severe headache with concerning changes, markedly reduced fetal movement when applicable, fluid leakage, or signs of labor outside the plan. Never delay maternal emergency care in order to seek pastoral permission or reassurance. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
