    "safety": "An undiagnosed condition does not make new severe symptoms routine. Use emergency services for recognized danger signs and clearly communicate baseline symptoms, current changes, medicines, allergies, and prior records. Do not recommend experimental substances, abrupt treatment changes, or travel to unverified clinics, and report rapidly worsening function to the coordinating clinician. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
