    "safety": "Secrecy cannot be promised when life is at risk. Scripture, prayer, and companionship belong alongside—not in place of—urgent medical assessment and qualified crisis care. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Create a concrete safety plan naming warning signs, internal coping steps, people and places that reduce isolation, emergency contacts, professional care, and how access to tools or substances will be reduced. Inspect and medically treat wounds. Reassess risk at every contact; a denial of suicidal intent does not make repeated or escalating injury low risk.",
