    "safety": "Do not require confrontation with an unsafe leader, route every report back through implicated authority, weaponize submission, or prioritize institutional reputation over truth and protection. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Map the authority structure, control of information, demanded secrecy, threats of divine judgment, retaliation, financial or sexual exploitation, misuse of discipline, and barriers to leaving or appealing. Use reviewers outside the implicated chain of command, protect records and complainants, and examine whether theology is being selectively deployed to immunize leadership from biblical accountability.",
