    "safety": "Sudden facial droop, arm or leg weakness, speech trouble, confusion, vision change, loss of balance, or severe unexplained headache requires an immediate emergency call even if symptoms improve. Note when the person was last known well, do not give food, drink, aspirin, or medication unless emergency professionals instruct it, and do not drive instead of using an ambulance. Pastoral caregivers must not diagnose, prescribe, change medication or equipment, interpret tests, promise healing, or recommend that prayer, fasting, supplements, essential oils, diets, or alternative practices replace qualified care. When danger may be present, stay with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or clinical service, preserve clear access for responders, and continue pastoral presence alongside—not instead of—professional treatment.",
    "_id": "stroke"
