    "safety": "Do not debate, shame, dare, minimize, or promise secrecy. Pastoral hope and Scripture must accompany immediate crisis and medical care rather than delay it. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. A high-risk response must specify who is physically present, whether a plan and means exist, the timeframe, past attempts, intoxication, agitation, recent loss, protective relationships, emergency evaluation, transfer of care, and the next confirmed contact. Do not rely on a no-harm promise. Document the questions, answers, consultation, actions, handoff, and follow-up while sharing information only with people needed to preserve life.",
