    "safety": "Detailed retelling, confrontation, forgiveness, or reconciliation must not be coerced; severe symptoms and danger call for trauma-competent medical or licensed care alongside pastoral ministry. Ask direct questions when danger may be present. If there is imminent risk, serious injury, abuse of a child or vulnerable adult, credible violence, dangerous withdrawal, or inability to maintain basic safety, remain with the person when safe, contact the appropriate emergency or civil authority, and involve qualified medical or licensed care. Pastoral care should continue alongside those protections. Stabilization precedes detailed processing. Assess ongoing threat, dissociation, flashbacks, nightmares, panic, substance use, self-harm, medical injury, housing, and contact with the perpetrator. Give the sufferer meaningful choices, avoid surprise touch or forced detail, teach grounding without implying the body is spiritually defective, and coordinate with trauma-competent care when symptoms exceed pastoral competence.",
