    "safety": "Do not use covert narcissism as a shortcut for disbelieving a woman, interpreting emotion as manipulation, or reframing reports of abuse as mutual conflict. Screen separately for coercive control, stalking, sexual coercion, threats, strangulation history, weapon access, child or elder harm, financial restriction, retaliation, and suicidal intent. If the counselee uses self-harm threats, false allegations, children, medical neglect, or access to basic needs to control another person, treat the conduct as a concrete safety issue rather than merely a trait. Preserve evidence lawfully, explain confidentiality limits, consult qualified advocates and clinicians, and report where required. Conjoint counseling is unsafe while coercion, intimidation, or material retaliation is active. A diagnosis never excuses abuse, and an unlicensed helper should not diagnose NPD.",
