    "safety": "Do not confuse female authority, assertiveness, success, boundaries, anger about injustice, or resistance to abuse with narcissism. Conversely, do not excuse coercion because it is expressed through social influence, sexuality, maternal authority, spiritual reputation, or institutional competence. Screen privately for partner violence, child abuse, sexual coercion, stalking, threats, financial exploitation, reputational retaliation, weapon access, and suicidal or homicidal intent. Protect complainants and witnesses, preserve evidence lawfully, disclose conflicts of interest, and use independent review where the woman holds leadership or social power. Couples counseling is inappropriate while coercive control or retaliation is active. Diagnosis does not determine whether protection or reporting is required; established conduct does.",
