    "safety": "Do not assume a withdrawn, ashamed, unemployed, depressed, disabled, or conflict-avoidant man is abusive or narcissistic. Also do not minimize coercive control because it is carried through silence, financial abandonment, threats of disappearance or self-harm, sexual pressure, spiritual neglect, sabotage, or selective incompetence. Screen privately for partner violence in either direction, child neglect, stalking, weapons, strangulation history, substance use, dangerous driving, suicidal or homicidal intent, and control of money, medication, housing, or transportation. A male victim must receive the same factual hearing and protection as any other victim. Active coercion or retaliation rules out conjoint counseling. Diagnosis is not required to address proven danger, and pastoral care must not replace licensed, medical, or civil intervention.",
